// AT MOST ONCE PER SELECT (design/wake_catchup.md): in1 fires while
// arm 0 (which does not read it) is selected — the bit is HELD. Arm 1
// wakes first and consumes it (count = 1, the catch-up fire). Arm 2
// wakes second: the bit is spent, its count receives present-but-
// stale, never a fire — its count has no value and the arm bottoms.
// The kernel had two fired-at-wake channels here (the aug08b arm-init
// stale-mask suppression and DynCallSlot's first-dispatch arrival
// upgrade), both of which made the jit emit 101; wake views now
// deliver honest stale (wire bit 2 + the R2 genuine-init-only rule at
// the site's first dispatch).
// Expected trace (both engines): 0; <quiet>; 1; <bottom>.
// schedule-v1: cap=208 events=1664; in1=i64:5; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:2
{let v0 = select in0 {i64:0 => i64:0, i64:1 => count(in1), i64:2 => count(in1) + i64:100, _ => i64:-1}; v0}
